title: 'Decided: the AI reader previews only a server that says it can, since an older one would save for real.'
pid: ee70e123-05a6-401c-8c52-64bc7a376885
body: |2-
  A server ignores a request field it does not know, so a preview sent
  to a server built before 2026-11-14 is an ordinary save: a dry run
  that writes. So "verify connection" now answers '(supports ("save
  preview"))', the tool asks it before each preview, and an older server
  gets no preview and a line saying so. Found while writing these notes,
  through a daemon still running the old tool against the team's old
  server, which happened to send no preview. The other way: a request of
  its own for the preview, which an older server refuses; but it refuses
  the request line and then reads the envelope as more requests, out of
  step on a daemon's connection.
